tion":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1732720779,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNzMyNzIwNzc5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gui","name":"topic:gui","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":5,"created_at":"2025-03-15T00:54:16Z","updated_at":"2025-03-17T15:52:02Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nGodot 4.4-stable, Godot 4.4.1rc1\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 10 with a 1920 by 1080 Monitor\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe click_mask of a texture button is offset vertically if the window size is 1920 by 1080. \n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nFirst create a scene with a CanvasLayer->Control. Set the anchor preset to full rect. Add a TextureButton add the hover texture the normal texture and the pressed texture then add a bitmap for the click_mask that matches the texture size of the normal texture. Then set the project settings window size to 1920 by 1080. Then go to the control node and reset the full rect again so it matches the window size.\n### Video \n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d04c4040-09d2-4b5b-97fb-b5046d3d97dc\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[TestingMRP.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19256346/TestingMRP.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104157/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104157/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":nul